# The dynamic-security state and anything the plugin writes beside it.
#
# THIS REPOSITORY IS PUBLIC. `dynamic-security.json` holds the broker's client
# list and password hashes, and on Mosquitto 2.1.x a broker that starts without
# it generates its own plus a `.pw` file containing passwords IN PLAINTEXT. A
# committed dev key or admin password is a permanent leak - git history keeps it
# after the file is deleted.
#
# These live on a named Docker volume in dev, so nothing should appear here at
# all; the rule exists for the day someone bind-mounts it to look inside.
data/
certs/
*.pw
dynamic-security.json
